<article class="env-lemma" id="0A75">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A75">Lemma <span data-tag="0A75">48.9.1</span>.</a> With notation as above. The functor $\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits (\mathcal{O}_ Z, -)$ is a right adjoint to the functor $i_* : \textit{Mod}(\mathcal{O}_ Z) \to \textit{Mod}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. For $V \subset Z$ open we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Gamma (V, \mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits (\mathcal{O}_ Z, \mathcal{F})) = \{ s \in \Gamma (U, \mathcal{F}) \mid \mathcal{I}s = 0\}   \]
</div>
  <p> where $U \subset X$ is an open whose intersection with $Z$ is $V$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_ Z$-modules. Then 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}_ X}(i_*\mathcal{G}, \mathcal{F}) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{i_*\mathcal{O}_ Z}(i_*\mathcal{G}, \mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}_ X}(i_*\mathcal{O}_ Z, \mathcal{F})) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}_ Z}(\mathcal{G}, \mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits (\mathcal{O}_ Z, \mathcal{F}))  \]
</div>
    <p>
       The first equality by Modules, Lemma <a href="/tag/0A6F" data-tag="0A6F">17.22.3</a> and the second by the fully faithfulness of $i_*$, see Modules, Lemma <a href="/tag/08KS" data-tag="08KS">17.13.4</a>. The description of sections is left to the reader. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>